{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794860572,"nonce":"0gVFoXU3CcCnhcxL7MZbkk9j/VY=","title":"A turned SVG under rows is culled by the rect it was painted at","message":"cn_demo Tree View: the chevrons of open items (`.cn-tree-item[data-state=\"open\"] .cn-tree-chevron { transform: rotate(90deg) }`) vanished while the page scrolled on rows and came back at rest.\n\nCause: `NodeRows::place_svg` folds the rows' move into an SVG's `css_affine` and leaves its rect at the painted pose, while its clip is moved. `render_rasterized_svgs` culled an SVG by testing that rect against the clip, ignoring the transform, so once the content had moved further than the icon's distance to its clip edge, the icon was dropped.\n\nFix: cull by the bounds the SVG is drawn at (`drawn_bounds`: the box around the transformed rect, placed as the instance is). Reproduced headlessly with `cn_demo_costs` `COSTS_AT=22200 COSTS_SNAP_SCROLL=\u003cpng\u003e` (sync decode); the scroll distance since the last full paint decides it, which is why async runs reproduced rarely. Guarded by the animation_paths scene \"scroll turned icons\" (6/16 frames differ with the old cull).","files":null}]}